    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-52-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(2) However, if:  (a) the Minister makes a decision under section 24 to refuse to approve a person becoming an Australian citizen; and  (b) the Minister’s reasons for the decision did not refer to the eligibility ground in subsection 21(8) (about statelessness); a person (the applicant) cannot apply for review of that decision unless the applicant is a permanent resident.",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@type": "xsd:decimal",
        "@value": "1.0000"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits review of decision for refusing citizenship application by applicant over 18.",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) However, if:  (a) the Minister makes a decision under section 24 to refuse to approve a person becoming an Australian citizen; and  (b) the Minister’s reasons for the decision did not refer to the eligibility ground in subsection 21(8) (about statelessness); a person (the applicant) cannot apply for review of that decision unless the applicant is a permanent resident."
    },
